  "semanticRules": [
    "Some/None and Ok/Err are each exhaustive closed two-variant families for their concrete type.",
    "A match evaluates its subject once and only its selected arm is evaluated.",
    "Some/Ok/Err bind one signed-i64 payload; None cannot bind a payload.",
    "Payload captures are lexically scoped to their arm. Nested matches may refer to outer captures.",
    "Duplicate, mixed, missing or wildcard-substitute ADT variants and incompatible subject or result types are compile errors.",
    "The zero-capability pure fixture does not specify cross-backend in-memory tags, wire formats, ownership, or actor transfers.",
    "Selected-arm-only evaluation is checked by inactive branches that would raise checked integer remainder by zero if evaluated."
  ],
